<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">19 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 19 June, from 1269 to 1961.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1269 CE <span class="tih-ago">757 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Louis IX orders Jews in France to wear a badge</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An ordinance of Louis IX required Jews to wear a coloured circle of cloth, the rouelle, on their clothing. It enforced a rule of the Fourth Lateran Council of 1215 and marked Jews out for discrimination.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1865 CE <span class="tih-ago">161 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Union troops proclaim emancipation in Galveston, Texas</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">General Gordon Granger announced that all enslaved people in Texas were free, two and a half years after the Emancipation Proclamation. The day is celebrated as Juneteenth, a US federal holiday since 2021.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/mexico" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mexico.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1867 CE <span class="tih-ago">159 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Emperor Maximilian of Mexico is executed</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Maximilian, the Austrian archduke installed by France as Emperor of Mexico, was shot by firing squad at Querétaro with two of his generals. Benito Juárez's republic was restored.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1910 CE <span class="tih-ago">116 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">First Father's Day is held in Spokane</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Sonora Smart Dodd organised the celebration to honour her father, a widower who raised six children. Father's Day became a permanent US national holiday in 1972.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1953 CE <span class="tih-ago">73 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Julius and Ethel Rosenberg are executed</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The couple were electrocuted at Sing Sing for passing atomic secrets to the Soviet Union. Ethel's role, in particular, remains disputed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1961 CE <span class="tih-ago">65 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Kuwait gains independence from Britain</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An exchange of notes ended the 1899 agreement that made Kuwait a British protectorate. Iraq claimed the new state, and invaded it in 1990.</p></div></li></ol>
